.TH COMMAND * 2014-04-08 "SequoiaDB" "Sequoiadb Method's Manual"
.ad l.ll 72.ce 1000
\fBrg.attachNode()\fR
.ce 0
.sp 2

.SH "NAME"

.sp 2
attachNode - Add a node that has been created but does not belong to any group to the current group.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp 2

.sp 2

.sp 2
rg.attachNode(\fB<host>\fR,\fB<service>\fR,\fB[options]\fR)
.SH "CATEGORY"

.sp 2

.sp 2
ReplicaGroup
.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.sp 2
Add a node that has been created but does not belong to any group to the current group. Can be used with rg.detachNode().

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp 2
\fBhost (string)\fR
.br
       Specify the host name of the node.
.sp 2
\fBservice (string)\fR
.br
       Node port number.
.sp 2
\fBoptions (json)\fR
.br
       Can be the following options:
.sp 2
       \fB1. KeepData (Bool):\fR 
.br
			  Whether to keep the original data of the 
			  current node, default to be false.
\fBNote: \fR
.sp 2
1. Never open KeepData if the node does not originally belong to the current group.
.sp 2
2. Nodes in the node configuration file where roles are specified as catalogs can only be added to the catalog group; nodes whose roles are specified as data can only be added to data groups.
			  
.SH "Examples"

.sp 2
1. Detach node from group1 and then add it to group2.
.sp 2
	> var rg1 = db.getRG("group1")
.br
	> rg1.detachNode('hostname1', '11830')
.br
	> var rg2 = db.getRG("group2")
.br
	> rg2.attachNode('hostname1', '11830')
